    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d461">

                <pb facs="0525" n="517" sameAs="frus:frus1939v02/pg517"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851.248/185: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Bullitt</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-04-26T17:00:00-05:00">April 26, 1939—5 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>313. Your No. 817, April 25, 9 a.m. I assume that the Minister for Air, in
                    connection with his plans for the purchase of Allison engines, is bearing in
                    mind the provisions of Section 1 (<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>) and Section 5
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">g</hi>) of the Neutrality Act.<anchor n="51"
                        xml:id="d461-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
